# AICL Example: Energy Trading Platform
# A comprehensive energy trading platform with spot trading, futures, settlement,
# grid balancing, regulatory compliance, and renewable energy certificate management
# Demonstrates ALL 10 AICL language levels

# =============================================================================
# LEVEL 1 — Architecture (Mandatory)
# =============================================================================

Goal:
Create an energy trading platform supporting spot market trading, futures contracts, day-ahead and intraday auctions, settlement and clearing, grid balancing services, and regulatory compliance across multiple jurisdictions

Constraint:
All trades must comply with FERC and European energy market regulations

Constraint:
Trade execution latency must not exceed 50 milliseconds

Constraint:
Settlement must be completed within T+2 business days

Constraint:
System must handle at least 50000 transactions per hour during peak trading

Constraint:
All pricing data must be accurate to 4 decimal places per MWh

Constraint:
Renewable energy certificates must be tracked with full provenance chain

Risk:
Market data feed interruption

Recovery:
Switch to backup data provider and halt automated trading strategies

Risk:
Settlement failure due to insufficient collateral

Recovery:
Liquidate positions to cover shortfall and notify risk management team

Risk:
Grid frequency deviation beyond safe limits

Recovery:
Activate emergency balancing reserves and notify grid operator

Risk:
Counterparty default on futures contract

Recovery:
Trigger margin call and invoke clearing house guarantee fund

Risk:
Regulatory investigation triggered

Recovery:
Freeze affected accounts and compile full audit trail within 24 hours

Risk:
Price manipulation detection

Recovery:
Suspend suspicious accounts and report to market surveillance authority

Layer:
